  {
    "sha": "41411498c7f2b83755b681539d4fc0008e20765c",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOUTGiVdoAKDQxNDExNDk4YzdmMmI4Mzc1NWI2ODE1MzlkNGZjMDAwOGUyMDc2NWM",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Basam Ahmed",
        "email": "219071866+BasamAhmed640@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-09-14T03:19:22Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Basam Ahmed",
        "email": "219071866+BasamAhmed640@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-09-14T03:19:22Z"
      },
      "message": "Review Learn lessons with a parallel crew of scoped, checkpointed checks\n\nScholar now coordinates lesson review as a crew of small isolated checks, up\nto six at a time: a source-fidelity check per four-page window, an explanation\ncheck per lesson topic, figure/equation packets (at most six images, each crop\nwith its full page) and one whole-lesson coherence check. Every page and current\ncrop is still inspected before approval, and an empty or unfinished crew can\nnever aggregate into a pass.\n\nEach passing check is cached by the exact packet it saw and saved to the note as\nsoon as it finishes, so an interruption, timeout or local edit re-runs only the\naffected checks. Checkpoint writes are drained before the approval write.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
